    <div class="rule-section">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Army Organisation Plan (AOP)</span></div>
      <table class="ref-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Slots (Pitched Battle)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/hq.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> HQ</td><td>1–2</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/troops.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Troops</td><td>2–6</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/elites.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Elites</td><td>0–3</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/fast-attack.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Fast Attack</td><td>0–3</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/heavy-support.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Heavy Support</td><td>0–3</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/dedicated-transport.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Dedicated Transport</td><td>0–ᵀ (one per Infantry unit)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/fortification.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Fortification</td><td>0–1</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/slot-icons/flyer.svg" class="slot-icon" alt=""> Flyer</td><td>0–2</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Minimum requirements:</strong> At least 1 HQ + 2 Troops + ≥25% of total points spent on Troops.</li>
        <li><strong>Exceeding AOP:</strong> When all slots are filled, gain a second identical AOP (same minimums apply). Transports, Fortifications, and Flyers don't need to be filled to trigger this.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Alliance Levels</span></div>
      <div class="alliance-grid">
        <div class="alliance-card alliance-card--g">
          <div class="alliance-badge"><span class="dot dot-g"></span> Battle Brothers</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Allied units are treated as friendly in all respects.</li>
            <li>Auras and psychic powers can be cast on allied units.</li>
            <li>Transport vehicles can carry units from both factions freely.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="alliance-card alliance-card--y">
          <div class="alliance-badge"><span class="dot dot-y"></span> Allies of Convenience</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Allied units are treated as separate armies.</li>
            <li>Auras and psychic powers only affect the primary faction's units.</li>
            <li>Transports can only carry units of the primary faction.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="alliance-card alliance-card--r">
          <div class="alliance-badge"><span class="dot dot-r"></span> Desperate Allies</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Same restrictions as Allies of Convenience, plus:</li>
            <li>Units within 12″ of the ally must pass a Ld test (−1) or lose their order for that turn.</li>
            <li>Uses own mini-AOP: 0–1 HQ · 1–2 Troops · 0–1 Elite/FA/HS per Troop · 0–ᵀ Transports.</li>
            <li>Cannot select a second AOP after filling all slots.</li>
            <li>May select own Army Customisation options.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">A faction may always ally with itself. Two Inquisition forces or two Dark Eldar Kabals allied together count as Allies of Convenience (Y), not Battle Brothers.</p>
