    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Allied Detachment AOP</span></div>
      <p class="section-note">Allies use their own Army Organization Plan, sharing only the army's point pool:</p>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>0–1 HQ</li>
        <li>1–2 Troops</li>
        <li>0–1 Elite*</li>
        <li>0–1 Fast Attack*</li>
        <li>0–1 Heavy Support*</li>
        <li>0–ᵀ Transports</li>
        <li>* For each Troop unit, one Elite, Fast Attack, or Heavy Support unit may be chosen.</li>
        <li>Allies cannot select a second AOP after filling all available slots.</li>
        <li>Allies may select their own Army Customisation options.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><strong>Allying with the same faction:</strong> a faction may ally with itself. Both parts are considered one army, so "Unique" equipment or "once per army" upgrades (like HQ selections) can still only be taken once.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>Limitation:</strong> units in an allied detachment can never make use of the "Objective secured!" rule.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Setting Up Units</span></div>
      <p class="section-note">Both players compare their total unit count. For every 2-unit difference, the player with fewer units receives a <strong>pass marker</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Deployment sequence:</strong> the player who won the side pick begins. Starting with them, players alternate placing one unit (with any attached characters) in their deployment zone. Instead of placing a unit, a player may:</p>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Board a transport:</strong> announce a unit is embarking and place the transport with any units (including attached characters).</li>
        <li><strong>Start in reserve:</strong> the unit enters the battlefield later.</li>
        <li><strong>Character joins a reserve unit:</strong> announce a character joins a unit held in reserve.</li>
        <li><strong>Infiltration:</strong> the unit is set up as an infiltrator and placed later.</li>
        <li><strong>Character joins an infiltrator unit:</strong> announce a character joins a unit as infiltrators.</li>
        <li><strong>Fortification setup:</strong> remove a piece of terrain at least 50% within your deployment zone and replace it with a Fortification-type unit.</li>
        <li><strong>Pass marker:</strong> skip a unit placement. After using a pass marker once, the player must deploy a unit next.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><strong>Infiltrators</strong> are placed alternately, the same way as normal units, after all other units are deployed. They do not count when determining the initiative bonus for the game. Some missions may outrule reserve or infiltrator options — always check the mission first.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Playing Your First Game</span></div>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Game size:</strong> 2500 points per player.</li>
        <li><strong>Table size:</strong> 72″ × 48″.</li>
        <li><strong>Mission:</strong> Take &amp; Hold.</li>
        <li>Skip the Army Customisation options at first — use the datasheets as written.</li>
        <li>Go easy on vehicle use for both sides.</li>
        <li>For a smaller game, use the Skirmish rules in the Mission Supplement (with unit limitations to keep it balanced).</li>
        <li>It is strongly recommended to use the Mission Supplement — the game is balanced around objective-based play.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /tab-army -->


  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- TAB: PSYCHIC                                               -->
  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div id="tab-psychic" class="tab-panel">

    <div class="rule-section">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Casting Psychic Powers</span></div>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Models with the <strong>Psyker</strong> rule can manifest psychic powers.</li>
        <li>Powers are classified as <strong>Basic</strong>, <strong>Normal</strong>, or <strong>Complex</strong> — see each order for which categories can be cast.</li>
        <li>Roll 2D6. Result must meet or exceed the power's cast value.</li>
        <li>Casting the same power again in the same turn: −1 cumulative penalty per attempt.</li>
        <li>Requires LOS to target unless stated otherwise.</li>
        <li>Psykers have access to the General Disciplines and their Codex disciplines.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Overchanneling</span></div>
      <p>May roll an extra die (3D6 total) when manifesting a power. Suffers D3 Mortal Wounds on any double (in addition to any Perils of the Warp).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Dispelling</span></div>
      <p>Some models may dispel powers. If an enemy psyker within 24″ successfully manifests a power: roll 2D6. Result must be <em>greater</em> than the psychic test result to dispel. Dispelled powers have no effect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Psychic Powers in Melee</span></div>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Psykers in melee can only cast <strong>basic</strong> psychic powers during their initiative phase.</li>
        <li>Targets limited to: the psyker, or friendly/enemy units in the same melee.</li>
        <li>Psykers not in melee cannot target units in melee with Witchfire powers.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Hymns, Invocations &amp; Prayers</span></div>
      <p>Cannot be dispelled. May only be attempted once per battle round per unit. If the user is eliminated, effects persist until the Rally phase of the next battle round.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Perils of the Warp</span></div>
      <p>Triggered on a double 1 or double 6 during the psychic test. Roll 1D6:</p>
      <table class="ref-table">
        <thead><tr><th>D6</th><th>Name</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td class="result-label">Sucked into the Warp</td><td>Pass Ld value test: 1 Mortal Wound. Fail: removed as casualty.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td class="result-label">Mindsteal</td><td>1 Mortal Wound. The attempted power cannot be used for the rest of the game.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td class="result-label">Power Drain</td><td>1 Mortal Wound. Roll 1D3: both players subtract result from all psychic tests for the rest of the round (cumulative).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td class="result-label">Psionic Feedback</td><td>1 Mortal Wound.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td class="result-label">Empyrian Aftermath</td><td>Fail Ld value test: 1 Mortal Wound.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>6</td><td class="result-label result-good">Warp Boost</td><td>Pass Ld value test: +1 to hit and +1 to wound rolls until end of next activation. Fail: 1 Mortal Wound.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">Vehicles use Leadership 10 for Perils tests. Fearless models still must pass Leadership <em>value</em> tests.</p>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /tab-psychic -->

</div><!-- /rules-page -->
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  var btns = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn');
  var panels = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-panel');
  btns.forEach(function (btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var id = btn.getAttribute('data-tab');
      btns.forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('tab-active'); });
      panels.forEach(function (p) { p.classList.remove('tab-panel--active'); });
      btn.classList.add('tab-active');
      var panel = document.getElementById('tab-' + id);
      if (panel) {
        panel.classList.add('tab-panel--active');
        // Reveal this tab's sections now. They were display:none when the observer ran, and an
        // IntersectionObserver never fires for a hidden element, so without this they stay at
        // opacity 0 until a scroll happens to catch them — which read as the page half-keeping
        // the previous tab.
        panel.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('visible'); });
      }
    });
  });
})();
</script>

